# Build output
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Test / benchmark scratch output (generated packages are written here)
tmp/
coverage/
bench/out/
bench/capacity/
# The campaign runner writes its logs here. They are working output: what the
# campaign established lives in qualification/, and the logs are kept on the
# machine that ran it.
bench/campaign/

# The offline universe writes one log per step here, and the report names each
# by path and digest. They are working output of the run, not part of the
# candidate — and until they were ignored the universe dirtied the tree it then
# required to be clean, so the sabotage step refused itself.
qualification/candidate/universe-logs/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Never commit environment material
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Scratch a run spills into, wherever a host puts it.
#
# Named for every shape it takes: the acceptance builder's directory beside each
# case, the CLI's directory beside its output, the staging directory a package is
# built in before it is published, and the run directory a store creates inside
# whatever root it was given. Scratch holds customer data; a copy of it that
# survives the run is a copy nothing later knows to delete, and one inside a
# repository is one that gets committed by the next `git add -A`.
acceptance/*/work/
*.kauro-work/
*.kauro-staging/
kauro-scratch-*/
